Core/Jessie: When did people start noticing? That something was wrong?
Core/Rose: Farm workers. They were the first ones showing symptoms, but most of them couldn’t afford to see a doctor.
Core/Jessie: So it just… spread.
Core/Rose: By the time anyone in the city hospitals caught on, half the produce supply was already contaminated.
Core/Jessie: Christ.
Core/Rose: It moved faster than anyone predicted. Pollination season didn’t help.